Read CLAUDE.md and the current repo.

Audit the Sprint 0.1 foundation against its specification. Do NOT add
features. For each item below, verify and report PASS/FAIL with file:line
evidence. Fix only FAILs.

1. set_tenant() uses set_config(..., true) — transaction-scoped, not session.
2. current_tenant() uses current_setting('app.tenant_id', true) and returns
   NULL (not an error, not '') when unset.
3. Every table has ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY and FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY.
4. Every RLS policy uses current_tenant() in both USING and WITH CHECK, so
   missing context yields zero rows and rejected writes (fail closed).
5. set_tenant() and current_tenant() are SECURITY INVOKER (not DEFINER).
6. TenantTx.WithTenant returns ErrNoTenant when tenant.From fails.
7. AuthMiddleware rejects authenticated users with missing tenant claim
   with 403, not an implicit global grant.
8. AssertNotPrivileged rejects superuser, app_migrator, BYPASSRLS roles,
   and table owners at boot.
9. Tables are owned by app_migrator; app_user owns nothing (table owners
   bypass grants and, without FORCE, RLS).
10. No package outside internal/db imports pgxpool.
11. Every service in docker-compose.yml has both mem_limit and cpus, every
    image is pinned, and `make budget` passes.
12. tests/tenant_isolation_test.go covers all four required subtests and
    connects as app_user.
13. deploy/initdb/01-roles.sql grants app_user only SELECT on tenants and
    SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on accounts (no DDL), and no role has
    BYPASSRLS.
14. accounts has UNIQUE (tenant_id, id) so later composite FKs can target it.
15. No log line emits request bodies, emails, or tokens.

If any FAIL requires a schema change, produce a new migration rather than
editing 000001. Report at the end: PASS/FAIL table, list of changes made,
and any items you could not verify.
